{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ושבח</b> [better off]. And ושבח is an adjective, like ירא אני, and the ח of חי״ת [the word] opens [with a dagesh] because it is among the throat letters." "<b>עדן</b>. Defective of heh; it is עד הנה [up to here]. And this matter, that he said the dead are more praiseworthy than the living, is against the oppressed — for every person accepts all that comes upon him from heaven, but cannot bear oppression done to him by a human being who is like him, and would choose death over life."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:26.321476801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}